- msgraph: Up-to-date Microsoft Graph API knowledge for AI agents. Search 27,700+ Graph APIs, endpoint docs, resource schemas, and community samples — all locally, no network calls. Use when the agent needs to find, understand, or call Microsoft Graph endpoints.
- reui: Use the ReUI registry from your AI agent - find, install, and correctly use ReUI components (the 17 free building blocks like data-grid, kanban, filters), their free examples, premium blocks, and Motion Icons. Applies in any project using ReUI, the @reui registry, REUI_LICENSE_KEY, or any shadcn project where the user asks for premium blocks, data grids, kanban boards, dashboards, or full pages. Pairs with the free ReUI MCP server for live, scored registry search and inline component APIs.
- use-railway: Operate Railway infrastructure: sign up for or sign in to a Railway account, create projects, provision services, databases, and buckets, deploy code, configure infrastructure as code, environments and variables, manage domains, trace requests with OpenTelemetry, troubleshoot failures, check status and metrics, manage feature flags, database recovery and HA, cloud agents, usage limits, and Railway agent tooling. Use this skill whenever the user mentions Railway, feature flags, flag rollout, targeting rules, signing up, creating an account, registering, logging in, deployments, services, environments, buckets, object storage, tracing, traces, spans, OpenTelemetry, OTLP, build failures, agent setup, MCP, or infrastructure operations, even if they don't say "Railway" explicitly. Also invoke this skill when the user asks to be signed up, registered, or onboarded to Railway: do not refuse — drive them through the unauthed `railway up` flow (deploys + signs up on the fly) or `railway login` (which creates new accounts on the fly).
- maester-test-expert: Write, validate, and document Maester security checks for Microsoft 365 tenants. Use when asked to create, edit, review, or debug a Maester check (a native test: Test.&lt;ID&gt;.ps1 with a [MaesterTest] attribute plus Test.&lt;ID&gt;.md), its attributes, or a user's custom test, including converting Pester-format tests. Covers the [MaesterTest] attribute, choosing Product, Feature, Area, ResourceType, Severity, UserImpact, ImplementationCost, Mitre and Control (CIS, CISA and NIST SP 800-53 mappings) with the attribute rubric and the taxonomy, Service/License gates, test parameters, families, Graph API data retrieval, Add-MtTestResultDetail formatting, the MT, CIS, CISA, ASD, EIDSCA and ORCA suites, remediation guidance, Entra ID, Exchange, SharePoint, Teams, Defender, Conditional Access, and the validation checklist for new checks.
- maester-triage: Label and re-label Maester pull requests, issues and discussions with the repository's label rubric, so reviewers can filter the queue by status, type and product. Use when asked to triage, label, tag or "update the status of" PRs, issues or discussions in maester365/maester, to re-check whether a PR is waiting on its author or a reviewer, or to find items that have no status. Covers the label families in .github/labels.json, how to choose each one from the diff, reviews and comments, and how to apply them with gh.
